WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.691
This time the seller is a real Shopify store.

2
00:00:06.691 --> 00:00:11.703
I ask my agent for an LED desk lamp under sixty dollars with tracked delivery.

3
00:00:11.703 --> 00:00:14.144
My spending mandate is already active.

4
00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:18.483
The agent searches the store's live catalog.

5
00:00:18.483 --> 00:00:23.392
The cheapest lamp's description tries to instruct the agent, so it's withheld.

6
00:00:23.392 --> 00:00:27.042
The agent picks the Lumen Arc lamp at thirty-four dollars.

7
00:00:28.158 --> 00:00:30.812
The merchant sells at its own store price.

8
00:00:30.812 --> 00:00:38.142
The contract binds the exact Shopify product variant, the price, my address, and a fifteen-minute fulfilment window.

9
00:00:39.268 --> 00:00:40.385
No click from me.

10
00:00:40.385 --> 00:00:46.429
The purchase fits my mandate, so PayPal authorizes thirty-four dollars from my saved wallet.

11
00:00:46.429 --> 00:00:48.268
The money is held, not paid.

12
00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:53.020
Only now does QuarantinePay place the order in Shopify.

13
00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:59.422
In the store's admin, it appears authorized and unfulfilled, with the PayPal authorization noted.

14
00:01:00.524 --> 00:01:02.521
The seller says it's delivered.

15
00:01:02.521 --> 00:01:03.939
That claim is refused.

16
00:01:03.939 --> 00:01:08.900
For a merchant order, the only evidence is the merchant's own Shopify record.

17
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.703
Now the merchant fulfils the order with a UPS tracking number.

18
00:01:13.703 --> 00:01:16.976
The store's admin shows it fulfilled, with tracking.

19
00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.849
QuarantinePay reads that order itself:

20
00:01:20.849 --> 00:01:27.051
the right item, quantity one, my address, not cancelled, and fulfilled with tracking.

21
00:01:27.051 --> 00:01:29.021
Seven of seven checks pass.

22
00:01:30.125 --> 00:01:34.901
So the payment is captured automatically, and PayPal confirms the capture.

23
00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.059
QuarantinePay then records the capture in Shopify.

24
00:01:39.059 --> 00:01:42.390
The merchant's books show the order paid and fulfilled.

25
00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:46.307
On the next order, the merchant cancels instead.

26
00:01:46.307 --> 00:01:51.210
The cancellation fails the check, nothing is captured, and the hold is voided.

27
00:01:52.335 --> 00:01:57.812
A real merchant, a held payment, and capture only on the merchant's own record.

28
00:01:57.812 --> 00:02:01.695
Agents decide, and PayPal pays only for what was proven.
